{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>With this shall Aharon come.</b> The reason Scripture mentions Aharon explicitly and did not rely on his having been mentioned at the beginning of the matter is that what preceded in the commandment applied only to Aharon alone — that he not enter and die — and this commandment does not pertain to anyone but him. But from here onward, the commandment applies not to Aharon alone but to all Israel as well, for it is a need of Israel that he enter the Holy of Holies to make atonement for them once a year, and the El would command His people to observe the statutes stated — that they bring Aharon in with a bull, etc., a holy linen tunic, etc. And they of blessed memory (Torat Kohanim ad loc.) interpreted [the phrase] as 'from that which is holy' — meaning the terumah of the chamber. Accordingly, Scripture is obliged to state the name of the commandment with a designation applicable to them [all]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:57:20.311983287Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}